Class 3-E: the assassination classroom.

00:00:39.542 --> 00:00:41.000
Here comes the second term...

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:43.792
Another day, another class bell rings.

00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:03.167
<i>You're all I think about</i>

00:01:03.167 --> 00:01:06.000
<i>Starting not to see anything else</i>

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:11.458
<i>I'll win your heart for sure--I swear</i>

00:01:11.458 --> 00:01:14.125
<i>Me, not cool? Oh, that old tale</i>

00:01:14.125 --> 00:01:16.833
<i>I've spared no effort since then</i>

00:01:16.833 --> 00:01:20.625
<i>Should be over my problems by now</i>

00:01:20.625 --> 00:01:24.625
<i>I'm brimming with confidence: I can do it</i>

00:01:24.625 --> 00:01:27.583
<i>And just when I get warmed up</i>

00:01:27.583 --> 00:01:32.792
<i>Yeah, I get knocked down like this every time</i>

00:01:32.792 --> 00:01:38.375
<i>Your scathing, serious voice cuts me</i>

00:01:38.375 --> 00:01:43.792
<i>Thousands, tens of thousands</i>
<i>of times I've given form to my feelings</i>

00:01:43.792 --> 00:01:49.292
<i>Driven them in,</i>
<i>thrown them in--but all you do is run</i>

00:01:49.292 --> 00:01:51.958
<i>Question, question: what</i>

00:01:51.958 --> 00:01:54.625
<i>Question, question: on earth</i>

00:01:54.625 --> 00:01:57.417
<i>Question, question: did I</i>

00:01:57.417 --> 00:02:00.000
<i>Ever know about you anyway?</i>

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:02.708
<i>Question, question: why</i>

00:02:02.708 --> 00:02:05.417
<i>Question, question: is it</i>

00:02:05.417 --> 00:02:08.250
<i>Question, question: you are</i>

00:02:08.250 --> 00:02:13.208
<i>So close and yet so far away?</i>

00:02:16.958 --> 00:02:20.958
"First Period: Summer Festival Time"
"by Hiroto Maehara"

00:02:23.042 --> 00:02:25.333
The last day of our special summer camp

00:02:25.333 --> 00:02:27.708
and our assassination vacation.

00:02:27.708 --> 00:02:32.083
We were making the most of
what was left of our time on the island.

00:02:32.083 --> 00:02:35.292
A test of courage? Now?

00:02:35.292 --> 00:02:39.292
Yes! What better activity
for a midsummer night?

00:02:39.292 --> 00:02:42.125
You just want to have some fun.

00:02:42.125 --> 00:02:43.917
Unlike <i>some </i>people,

00:02:43.917 --> 00:02:46.792
<i>I've </i>been cooped up
in a shell this whole time!

00:02:46.792 --> 00:02:49.083
On a tropical isle, of all places!

00:02:49.083 --> 00:02:51.375
A test of courage? Could be fun!

00:02:51.375 --> 00:02:52.292
Right?

00:02:52.292 --> 00:02:55.125
But I don't like scary stuff.

00:02:55.125 --> 00:02:58.500
No sweat!
Koro Sensei'll be playing the ghosts.

00:02:58.500 --> 00:03:00.125
Oh, right!

00:03:03.292 --> 00:03:05.875
We had no idea at the time

00:03:05.875 --> 00:03:06.000
"Matchmaking!!"
We had no idea at the time

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:10.708
"Matchmaking!!"
that our teacher had another, baser goal in mind.

00:03:10.708 --> 00:03:12.125
"Matchmaking!!"

00:03:12.625 --> 00:03:15.250
We'll hold it in this ocean cavern.

00:03:15.250 --> 00:03:18.708
Walk through to the exit in boy-girl pairs.

00:03:21.958 --> 00:03:25.000
Do you mind this kind of thing, Nagisa?

00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:31.667
Well, scary stuff doesn't bother me,
but I'm not much for jump scares.

00:03:31.667 --> 00:03:35.375
Koro Sensei's so fast, we could be in trouble

00:03:35.375 --> 00:03:37.875
if he really meant to scare us.

00:03:37.875 --> 00:03:41.042
Is that an Okinawa <i>shamisen</i>?

00:03:47.583 --> 00:03:49.083
There he is!

00:03:49.083 --> 00:03:54.125
This is a blood-drenched cave of tragedy...

00:03:54.125 --> 00:04:03.583
where Ryukyu royalty,
defeated in battle, met a violent end.

00:04:03.583 --> 00:04:05.375
Is it really?

00:04:05.375 --> 00:04:08.875
He probably just made it up
to make it feel more real.

00:04:08.875 --> 00:04:11.417
You must stay together.

00:04:11.417 --> 00:04:16.167
Wandering spirits will
haunt to death anyone left alone!

00:04:18.292 --> 00:04:21.250
Th-This is sounding pretty authentic.

00:04:21.250 --> 00:04:23.125
Let's hurry through, Nagisa.

00:04:23.125 --> 00:04:24.708
Uh-huh.

00:04:24.708 --> 00:04:27.333
--This is a blood-drenched cave of tragedy...

00:04:27.333 --> 00:04:28.750
--Hearing him tell the same story to the next couple
--This is a blood-drenched cave of tragedy...

00:04:28.750 --> 00:04:30.625
--Hearing him tell the same story to the next couple
--where Ryukyu royalty, defeated in battle...

00:04:30.625 --> 00:04:32.750
--makes it even more real.
--where Ryukyu royalty, defeated in battle...

00:04:35.708 --> 00:04:38.375
You've gotten so much stronger.

00:04:38.375 --> 00:04:42.375
But you're still missing a little something.

00:04:42.375 --> 00:04:43.542
And that is...

00:04:43.542 --> 00:04:43.917
"Matchmaking!!"
And that is...

00:04:43.917 --> 00:04:45.875
"Matchmaking!!"
A love scandal!

00:04:45.875 --> 00:04:46.042
"Tentacle"
A love scandal!

00:04:46.042 --> 00:04:49.583
"Tentacle"
A few couples may have formed by summertime,

00:04:49.583 --> 00:04:51.583
"Tentacle"
but you're so focused on assassination

00:04:51.583 --> 00:04:53.750
"Tentacle"
that there hasn't been a single scandalous tale!

00:04:53.750 --> 00:04:59.750
Here's where I use fear to give you a little push together.

00:04:59.750 --> 00:05:00.083
"Student Data"
Here's where I use fear to give you a little push together.

00:05:00.083 --> 00:05:01.792
"Student Data"
Then I can tease you--

00:05:01.792 --> 00:05:03.792
"Student Data"
or write a based-on-a-true-story novel!

00:05:03.792 --> 00:05:06.750
"Student Data"
Such is your teacher's generous consideration!

00:05:06.750 --> 00:05:07.375
"Koro Sensei's Weak Point #12: Juicy stories"
Such is your teacher's generous consideration!

00:05:07.375 --> 00:05:08.625
"Koro Sensei's Weak Point #12: Juicy stories"

00:05:09.792 --> 00:05:12.708
Afraid of being... unafraid?

00:05:12.708 --> 00:05:19.083
Yep. Seeing Nagisa just then?
Honestly, I was shocked.

00:05:21.167 --> 00:05:25.958
Not when he beat Takaoka. After that.

00:05:25.958 --> 00:05:28.792
He wasn't the slightest bit afraid.

00:05:28.792 --> 00:05:31.542
I mean, in a fight, I'd for sure win.

00:05:31.542 --> 00:05:36.125
But to an assassin,
that kind of victory doesn't mean squat.

00:05:36.125 --> 00:05:38.292
That's when I first realized

00:05:38.292 --> 00:05:42.333
I was actually most afraid of not being afraid.

00:05:43.625 --> 00:05:45.417
Still...

00:05:45.417 --> 00:05:47.500
I won't lose.

00:05:47.500 --> 00:05:52.125
I'll be the one to take that teacher's life.

00:05:52.125 --> 00:05:55.500
Uh-huh! Can't wait to see
who ends up killing him.

00:05:55.500 --> 00:05:57.000
Say...

00:05:57.000 --> 00:05:57.333
"The Famous Ryukyu Twister Game"
Say...

00:05:57.333 --> 00:05:59.167
"The Famous Ryukyu Twister Game"
This was a test of courage?

00:05:59.167 --> 00:06:03.500
"The Famous Ryukyu Twister Game"
'Cause it looks like he's got something stupid up his sleeve.

00:06:04.667 --> 00:06:09.875
These couples just aren't
coming together. The next one, for sure!

00:06:12.083 --> 00:06:17.708
This is a blood-drenched
cave of tragedy... where Ryukyu--

00:06:17.708 --> 00:06:19.708
Monster!

00:06:19.708 --> 00:06:22.958
I've been spooking people
out at night since I was a kid.

00:06:22.958 --> 00:06:27.208
They call me Miss Couragetester,
Japanese delegate.

00:06:27.208 --> 00:06:31.375
Well, uh... as long as you're havin' fun.

00:06:32.917 --> 00:06:34.750
Wh-What was that ghost I just saw?

00:06:34.750 --> 00:06:35.083
"Koro Sensei's Weak Point #24:"
Wh-What was that ghost I just saw?

00:06:35.083 --> 00:06:36.083
"Koro Sensei's Weak Point #24:"
Not the actual spirit of an actual Ryukyu ruler!

00:06:36.083 --> 00:06:37.375
"As expected, spooked by the supernatural"
Not the actual spirit of an actual Ryukyu ruler!

00:06:37.375 --> 00:06:38.542
Not the actual spirit of an actual Ryukyu ruler!

00:06:39.458 --> 00:06:41.083
No eyes!

00:06:41.083 --> 00:06:42.167
"His own konjac contraption"

00:06:42.375 --> 00:06:45.083
I just felt something slithery!

00:06:45.083 --> 00:06:47.167
A Japanese doll?!

00:06:47.167 --> 00:06:49.542
Horror cartoonist Shigeru Mizuki!

00:06:51.750 --> 00:06:55.458
Turns out he's enjoying the frights the most.

00:06:55.458 --> 00:06:57.875
Let's just get out of here.

00:07:00.250 --> 00:07:04.583
What a disgrace... what a total disgrace...

00:07:04.583 --> 00:07:07.708
So basically you meant to
frighten us into becoming couples

00:07:07.708 --> 00:07:10.167
thanks to the suspension-bridge effect?

00:07:10.167 --> 00:07:12.625
We saw right through you
before you even scared us!

00:07:12.625 --> 00:07:14.375
B-But I so wanted to see you all!

00:07:14.375 --> 00:07:17.125
I wanted to grin at you holding hands
and blushing, two by two!

00:07:17.125 --> 00:07:19.000
--I was trying to keep you from marrying someone random!

00:07:19.000 --> 00:07:20.667
--He's sobbing with frustration!
--I was trying to keep you from marrying someone random!

00:07:20.667 --> 00:07:22.333
What a shabby grown-up.

00:07:22.333 --> 00:07:25.250
Never mind that stuff.

00:07:25.250 --> 00:07:30.250
There are plenty of us who
don't want to be dragged into a love affair.

00:07:30.250 --> 00:07:33.875
We're not all as sleazy as you.

00:07:33.875 --> 00:07:37.500
All right, Nakamura. I get it.

00:07:37.500 --> 00:07:41.250
You call that a test of courage?
There was nobody in there!

00:07:41.250 --> 00:07:43.042
What a waste of fear!

00:07:43.042 --> 00:07:45.958
I told you it was pointless
clinging to me like that.

00:07:45.958 --> 00:07:47.917
I don't need that kind of baggage
after an all-nighter.

00:07:47.917 --> 00:07:50.208
Shut up! You're a man, aren't you?

00:07:50.208 --> 00:07:53.458
If there's a pretty woman around,
escort her nicely!

00:07:57.917 --> 00:08:01.292
Say... I'm starting to wonder...

00:08:01.292 --> 00:08:03.500
Is Professor Bitch...?

00:08:03.500 --> 00:08:04.500
Uh-huh.

00:08:04.500 --> 00:08:05.667
What should we do?

00:08:05.667 --> 00:08:09.667
We've got time before
we go home tomorrow morning.

00:08:09.667 --> 00:08:12.250
Shall we push them together?

00:08:12.250 --> 00:08:15.500
We <i>were </i>sleazy after all.

00:08:15.500 --> 00:08:19.292
And so our final operation was underway.

00:08:20.333 --> 00:08:22.333
Ugh! That does it!

00:08:22.333 --> 00:08:24.875
How obtuse can a person be?

00:08:24.875 --> 00:08:30.500
This isn't like you.
You wrap men around your little finger!

00:08:30.500 --> 00:08:33.542
But when it comes to her own love life,
she's inexperienced.

00:08:33.542 --> 00:08:36.625
Love? Ha! Don't make me laugh.

00:08:36.625 --> 00:08:38.250
What, it's not love?

00:08:38.250 --> 00:08:42.875
He's a rare bird, that's all--
a world-class square!

00:08:42.875 --> 00:08:48.250
And while I was all worked up,
trying to get him to fall for me,

00:08:48.250 --> 00:08:51.750
before I knew it, I...

00:08:52.500 --> 00:08:54.625
That was kinda cute.

00:08:54.625 --> 00:08:56.083
And a little humiliating.

00:08:56.083 --> 00:08:57.125
What? Why?

00:08:57.125 --> 00:09:00.750
Professor Bitch is
more awkward than she seems.

00:09:00.750 --> 00:09:05.208
All her experience must get in the way
of being true to her emotions.

00:09:05.208 --> 00:09:08.417
Then just leave it to us!

00:09:08.417 --> 00:09:10.917
We'll set the perfect stage for you two!

00:09:10.917 --> 00:09:13.000
Good idea!

00:09:13.000 --> 00:09:14.500
You kids...

00:09:14.500 --> 00:09:15.708
"Karasuma + Irina" "Pair-Up Plan"

00:09:16.333 --> 00:09:21.250
Let the Class 3-E love consultant
meeting come to order!

00:09:21.250 --> 00:09:22.542
Eager much, octopus?

00:09:22.542 --> 00:09:26.375
It's only natural to
encourage love between colleagues.

00:09:26.375 --> 00:09:29.917
A woman teacher's days of desire,
infatuated with a man...

00:09:29.917 --> 00:09:33.125
It's got the makings of
a bittersweet pure-romance novel!

00:09:33.125 --> 00:09:35.875
You're clearly planning something racier.

00:09:35.875 --> 00:09:40.417
First off, Professor Bitch, you dress all wrong.

00:09:40.417 --> 00:09:44.125
Totally. "If it's revealing, it's appealing"?

00:09:44.125 --> 00:09:48.167
That's not what a square
Japanese guy like Mr. Karasuma likes.

00:09:48.167 --> 00:09:51.292
You've got to be more... neatly dressed.

00:09:51.958 --> 00:09:53.625
Neatly dressed, eh?

00:09:53.625 --> 00:09:57.583
Yeah, like... Kanzaki.

00:09:57.583 --> 00:10:00.500
If yesterday's outfit is dry,
could you lend it to her?

00:10:00.500 --> 00:10:02.125
Yeah, sure.

00:10:02.708 --> 00:10:06.792
See? One piece of clothing
and you're nice and--

00:10:06.792 --> 00:10:09.417
H-How'd that make her <i>sexier</i>?!

00:10:09.417 --> 00:10:12.417
For starters, the fit's a little off in places.

00:10:12.417 --> 00:10:16.458
When I think of Kanzaki wearing
something sexy like that... whoo!

00:10:16.458 --> 00:10:19.667
Well, whatever. We can't fix the sexy.

00:10:19.667 --> 00:10:23.583
Compatibility is more important than boobs!

00:10:24.458 --> 00:10:27.583
Does anyone know Mr. Karasuma's type?

00:10:27.583 --> 00:10:33.208
Oh! He couldn't stop talking about
that one person in a TV commercial.

00:10:33.208 --> 00:10:35.708
Said she was his ideal type.

00:10:35.708 --> 00:10:40.958
Now <i>she's </i>a good one.
Expression, figure--both ideal.

00:10:40.958 --> 00:10:42.500
And there are three of them!

00:10:42.500 --> 00:10:44.583
Ideal military potential, he meant!

00:10:44.583 --> 00:10:47.833
Th-Then how about cooking for him?

00:10:47.833 --> 00:10:50.083
The hotel's dinners are plenty grand,

00:10:50.083 --> 00:10:53.833
but why not eat his favorite
dish together, just the two of you?

00:10:53.833 --> 00:10:58.042
I've only seen him eat burgers and cup ramen.

00:10:58.042 --> 00:11:01.667
That's just too pitiful for a one-on-one date.

00:11:02.500 --> 00:11:05.250
There's no in we can use
to push you together!

00:11:05.250 --> 00:11:09.417
I'm starting to think
Mr. Karasuma's the problem here.

00:11:09.417 --> 00:11:10.500
Right? Right?

00:11:10.500 --> 00:11:14.333
And he brushes off my jokes so coldly!

00:11:14.333 --> 00:11:18.500
With no options left,
we began dissing Mr. Karasuma.

00:11:18.500 --> 00:11:22.792
Let's just do what we can before dinner.

00:11:22.792 --> 00:11:24.958
The girls will assist with the styling,

00:11:24.958 --> 00:11:28.333
while the boys will get the mood
just right at their table.

00:11:28.333 --> 00:11:29.958
Roger!

00:11:36.417 --> 00:11:40.125
I thought we'd be eating as a group.
What's all this?

00:11:40.125 --> 00:11:43.333
No seats left for you, Mr. Karasuma.

00:11:43.333 --> 00:11:46.250
It's our famous E Class teacher bullying!

00:11:46.250 --> 00:11:52.250
You teachers just get in the way.
You can go eat outside.

00:11:54.750 --> 00:11:56.792
Where'd <i>that </i>come from?

00:11:56.792 --> 00:12:00.792
I just don't know what junior-high students
are thinking these days.

00:12:13.833 --> 00:12:16.042
Why were we the only ones kicked out?

00:12:16.042 --> 00:12:18.833
Oh, uh... you got me.

00:12:18.833 --> 00:12:20.708
What's with the shawl?

00:12:20.708 --> 00:12:23.333
I bought it at a shop,
borrowed a sewing machine,

00:12:23.333 --> 00:12:25.708
then used online photos
to fake a brand-name lookalike.

00:12:25.708 --> 00:12:28.083
Home ec always was your specialty.

00:12:28.083 --> 00:12:32.375
The field is set. Go get him, Professor Bitch!

00:12:33.917 --> 00:12:35.375
This shawl...

00:12:35.375 --> 00:12:39.250
It'd never fly in high society.

00:12:39.250 --> 00:12:42.250
And this table setting?
Clearly the work of an amateur.

00:12:42.250 --> 00:12:46.625
This is worlds apart from
the top-class places I used for work.

00:12:46.625 --> 00:12:51.500
And the gawkers! So much for privacy.

00:12:52.917 --> 00:12:55.083
And yet...

00:12:55.083 --> 00:12:58.917
What do you know? This is fun!

00:12:58.917 --> 00:13:03.417
I kind of love you guys! I'm going to do this!

00:13:03.417 --> 00:13:06.417
I'll take down this square--you'll see!

00:13:13.417 --> 00:13:16.750
A lot happened on this trip.

00:13:16.750 --> 00:13:19.250
But we did get results.

00:13:19.250 --> 00:13:24.417
In an unexpected way, I confirmed
that the students know their fundamentals.

00:13:25.000 --> 00:13:28.042
At this rate, we're sure to
kill him during the second term.

00:13:28.042 --> 00:13:32.167
I'm relying on your strength, too, Irina.

00:13:39.708 --> 00:13:41.333
What is it?

00:13:48.708 --> 00:13:53.417
Say, Karasuma...

00:13:53.417 --> 00:13:59.083
Do you really know what it means to kill?

00:14:03.000 --> 00:14:06.667
Well, <i>that </i>got somber fast.

00:14:06.667 --> 00:14:10.833
And look how you've jammed in your napkin.

00:14:23.542 --> 00:14:27.333
I like you, Karasuma. Good night.

00:14:36.875 --> 00:14:39.250
Stupid, stupid, stupid! Die, you dummy!

00:14:39.250 --> 00:14:40.125
You were supposed to tell him you love him,

00:14:40.125 --> 00:14:41.125
"Reveal killings" "Reveal feelings"
You were supposed to tell him you love him,

00:14:41.125 --> 00:14:42.500
"Reveal killings" "Reveal feelings"
not talk about killing!

00:14:42.500 --> 00:14:43.583
"Reveal killings" "Reveal feelings"
What kind of half-assed kiss was that?

00:14:43.583 --> 00:14:45.750
What kind of half-assed kiss was that?

00:14:45.750 --> 00:14:48.458
Use your tongue, your tongue!
Like you always do!

00:14:48.458 --> 00:14:53.333
You irritating brats!
Grown-ups have grown-up circumstances!

00:14:53.333 --> 00:14:55.792
It's okay--now she'll take her time to work on

00:14:55.792 --> 00:14:58.417
some decently indecent developments. Right?

00:14:58.417 --> 00:15:01.167
No, not "right," you octoperv!

00:15:03.292 --> 00:15:09.000
I won't give this too much thought.
After all, that's my duty.

00:15:09.000 --> 00:15:13.917
Prepare yourself. The second term:
this is when we train even harder.

00:15:13.917 --> 00:15:16.208
This is when we kill him.

00:15:16.208 --> 00:15:21.083
And so our assassination vacation
finally came to a close.

00:15:25.542 --> 00:15:28.750
But what was that at the end there?

00:15:28.750 --> 00:15:31.542
A new move? Impressive.

00:15:31.542 --> 00:15:33.875
"Mr. Karasuma's Weak Point #1: Denser than dense"

00:15:33.875 --> 00:15:37.875
"Assassination Classroom, Second Season"
"by Nagisa Shiota"

00:15:41.458 --> 00:15:42.583
We were all spending the last day of summer in our own ways.

00:15:42.583 --> 00:15:46.583
"Traditional Edo-Style Sushi-Go-Round"
We were all spending the last day of summer in our own ways.

00:15:49.667 --> 00:15:53.208
Getting along with Mom all right?

00:15:55.125 --> 00:15:58.250
Must be tough when she's so strict.

00:15:58.250 --> 00:16:02.333
I feel bad for bailing on you.

00:16:02.333 --> 00:16:07.833
It's okay. She's not so strict
if you don't tick her off.

00:16:07.833 --> 00:16:09.833
I see.

00:16:09.833 --> 00:16:11.750
But anyway, I--

00:16:11.750 --> 00:16:14.125
"Summer Festival!"

00:16:14.125 --> 00:16:14.708
"Summer Festival!"
What is it? Why'd you clam up?

00:16:14.708 --> 00:16:16.833
"If you're free at 7 tonight, meet at Kunugigaoka Station!"
What is it? Why'd you clam up?

00:16:16.833 --> 00:16:18.875
A summer festival?

00:16:19.958 --> 00:16:24.542
The last day of summer vacation:
Let's hang out and have some mindless fun!

00:16:27.375 --> 00:16:28.792
Thanks!

00:16:29.917 --> 00:16:31.458
Hey, uh, thanks for the sushi, Dad!

00:16:31.458 --> 00:16:33.625
Huh? Wait, you're done already?

00:16:33.625 --> 00:16:36.417
There's something I've got to do.

00:16:36.417 --> 00:16:40.042
See you! Take care of yourself and all that!

00:16:43.875 --> 00:16:44.333
"Kunugi Real Estate"

00:16:44.333 --> 00:16:47.333
"Kunugi Real Estate"
He's cheered up, that Nagisa.

00:16:48.083 --> 00:16:48.917
Huh?

00:16:48.917 --> 00:16:49.167
"Mode Select"
Huh?

00:16:49.167 --> 00:16:50.375
"Mode Select"
A festival?

00:16:50.375 --> 00:16:50.625
"Summer Festival!"
A festival?

00:16:50.625 --> 00:16:53.833
"Summer Festival!"
I just thought of it today. I'm asking everyone in class!

00:16:53.833 --> 00:16:57.583
"Summer Festival!"
So many have begged off with other plans that I'm feeling hurt.

00:16:57.583 --> 00:16:58.250
So many have begged off with other plans that I'm feeling hurt.

00:16:58.250 --> 00:16:59.500
Well...

00:16:59.500 --> 00:17:01.542
all right.

00:17:01.542 --> 00:17:04.583
I was just lazing around anyway.

00:17:05.750 --> 00:17:08.667
A festival, eh?

00:17:08.667 --> 00:17:11.958
I'm pleased my target
would think to invite me,

00:17:11.958 --> 00:17:15.750
but I'm afraid I'm out of Japan
on another job at the moment.

00:17:15.750 --> 00:17:17.875
I'll come pick you up!

00:17:17.875 --> 00:17:21.667
Mr. Karasuma's in a meeting
or something--no one'll be there!

00:17:21.667 --> 00:17:22.625
"Koro Sensei's Weak Point #25:"
Don't be silly. I'm working.

00:17:22.625 --> 00:17:24.500
"Thinks a poor turnout means he's worthless"
Don't be silly. I'm working.

00:17:24.500 --> 00:17:28.833
Well, all right.
Come by and kill me anytime, okay?

00:17:28.833 --> 00:17:30.792
But of course.

00:17:33.083 --> 00:17:36.125
From what Karasuma's told me,

00:17:36.125 --> 00:17:39.375
that boy pulled off
the secret move I taught him

00:17:39.375 --> 00:17:42.167
with no difficulty at all.

00:17:42.167 --> 00:17:46.083
Every country has its talent.

00:17:46.083 --> 00:17:49.750
Too bad I had to leave him in Japan.

00:17:56.167 --> 00:17:58.208
From the moment you were born,

00:17:58.208 --> 00:18:02.583
I've always been at your side.

00:18:11.333 --> 00:18:15.917
Fear not the name of the Reaper.

00:18:22.417 --> 00:18:24.042
I got a real good deal!

00:18:24.042 --> 00:18:25.458
Yesss!

00:18:27.917 --> 00:18:29.708
It's so fizzy!

00:18:29.708 --> 00:18:33.958
More came than I expected!
Excellent, excellent.

00:18:33.958 --> 00:18:37.625
I was considering suicide
if no one had shown up.

00:18:37.625 --> 00:18:40.750
I guess we shouldn't have come, then.

00:18:42.958 --> 00:18:46.542
Chiba and Hayami? Why so glum?

00:18:46.542 --> 00:18:48.958
We got banned from the shooting gallery.

00:18:48.958 --> 00:18:52.333
--It was too easy. We got carried away.

00:18:52.333 --> 00:18:54.250
--Hey, mister...
--It was too easy. We got carried away.

00:18:54.250 --> 00:18:56.417
I spent five thousand yen

00:18:56.417 --> 00:18:57.750
and never got any better than fifth place.

00:18:57.750 --> 00:18:58.125
"String Lottery" "Grand Prize" "1 Try: ¥250"
and never got any better than fifth place.

00:18:58.125 --> 00:18:59.958
"String Lottery" "Grand Prize" "1 Try: ¥250"
Going by the number of strings and prizes left,

00:18:59.958 --> 00:19:04.000
"String Lottery" "Grand Prize" "1 Try: ¥250"
the probability of never getting fourth-place or above is...

00:19:04.000 --> 00:19:09.208
Wow! 0.05 percent!
Are <i>any </i>of these strings a winner?

00:19:09.208 --> 00:19:12.042
Maybe I ought to get a police officer over here to check!

00:19:12.042 --> 00:19:12.542
"String Lottery" "Grand Prize"
Maybe I ought to get a police officer over here to check!

00:19:12.542 --> 00:19:13.792
"String Lottery" "Grand Prize"
All right, all right!

00:19:13.792 --> 00:19:14.750
"String Lottery" "Grand Prize"
You can have your money back--

00:19:14.750 --> 00:19:15.917
"String Lottery" "Grand Prize"
just keep your mouth shut, kid!

00:19:15.917 --> 00:19:16.875
"String Lottery" "Grand Prize"
Oh, no no no.

00:19:16.875 --> 00:19:20.000
"String Lottery" "Grand Prize"
I didn't spend five thousand yen to get my money back.

00:19:20.000 --> 00:19:21.833
"String Lottery" "Grand Prize"
I want a game console!

00:19:21.833 --> 00:19:24.208
"String Lottery" "Grand Prize"
Karma sure is persistent.

00:19:24.208 --> 00:19:27.917
"String Lottery" "Grand Prize"
He could tell from the start that none of 'em were big winners.

00:19:30.083 --> 00:19:33.542
There you go again, Isogai.
Is there anything you can't do?

00:19:33.542 --> 00:19:37.667
There's a knack to it.
It's a lot like slicing with a knife.

00:19:37.667 --> 00:19:39.708
That'll do.

00:19:39.708 --> 00:19:43.917
When you're poor, you're glad to get
a whole meal for a hundred yen.

00:19:43.917 --> 00:19:46.333
--Sure.
--Maybe a nice pan-fry...

00:19:46.333 --> 00:19:49.167
What? He's gonna <i>eat </i>those?

00:19:49.167 --> 00:19:51.250
Everyone's really raking it in, huh?

00:19:51.250 --> 00:19:55.708
Yeah--putting the subtleties
of our assassination skills to work.

00:19:55.708 --> 00:19:58.208
And Professor Bitch is in
the Chamber of Commerce tent,

00:19:58.208 --> 00:20:00.125
letting everyone buy her drinks.

00:20:00.125 --> 00:20:01.750
Where's Koro Sensei?

00:20:01.750 --> 00:20:06.167
He's always short on money
at the end of the month, so...

00:20:06.167 --> 00:20:08.542
He's running food stalls?!

00:20:08.542 --> 00:20:11.250
"Octopus Balls" "Old-Fashioned Candied Apricots" "Shaved Ice"
And he keeps branching out, too.

00:20:11.250 --> 00:20:15.125
"Octopus Balls" "Old-Fashioned Candied Apricots" "Shaved Ice"
He's moving into successful stalls that closed up early.

00:20:15.125 --> 00:20:16.333
"Octopus Balls" "Old-Fashioned Candied Apricots" "Shaved Ice"
I get it.

00:20:16.333 --> 00:20:19.625
"Octopus Balls" "Old-Fashioned Candied Apricots" "Shaved Ice"
So we unwittingly helped him earn his spending money.

00:20:19.625 --> 00:20:20.875
"Cotton Candy" "Big Servings, Fresh Flavor! Yakisoba & Hot Dogs"
So we unwittingly helped him earn his spending money.

00:20:29.458 --> 00:20:31.583
Wow!

00:20:31.583 --> 00:20:33.125
Nice!

00:20:33.125 --> 00:20:35.333
Gorgeous!

00:20:41.208 --> 00:20:44.375
Our summer break sure was packed.

00:20:44.375 --> 00:20:45.792
Yeah.

00:20:47.500 --> 00:20:52.750
But I bet our second term'll be
even more packed.

00:20:52.750 --> 00:20:56.750
If one person kills him,
the ten billion yen stands.

00:20:56.750 --> 00:20:58.250
But given the summer report

00:20:58.250 --> 00:21:01.958
indicating that group tactics had him cornered,

00:21:01.958 --> 00:21:06.667
a successful group assassination will reap a greater reward:

00:21:06.667 --> 00:21:07.000
"Wanted" "Max Reward: 30 Billion Yen"
a successful group assassination will reap a greater reward:

00:21:07.000 --> 00:21:12.208
"Wanted" "Max Reward: 30 Billion Yen"
an increased bounty of thirty billion yen.

00:21:15.292 --> 00:21:17.583
One thing we know for sure in this classroom

00:21:17.583 --> 00:21:22.708
is that we and Koro Sensei
won't be the same when it's over.

00:21:23.542 --> 00:21:28.292
As expected, the second term
will start with its ups and downs.

00:21:42.500 --> 00:21:48.000
<i>The moon that swims in the night sky</i>

00:21:48.000 --> 00:21:53.375
<i>If you stretch out your hand, you can reach it</i>

00:21:53.375 --> 00:21:59.042
<i>I went to touch it: it was warm</i>

00:21:59.042 --> 00:22:04.208
<i>And slowly drew me in</i>

00:22:04.208 --> 00:22:15.583
<i>The multiplying footsteps,</i>
<i>the view from my window:</i>

00:22:15.583 --> 00:22:21.167
<i>As I drifted along, expressionless</i>

00:22:21.167 --> 00:22:25.583
<i>They spilled out of my hands</i>

00:22:25.583 --> 00:22:32.417
<i>It was rocking, swaying--I never knew</i>

00:22:32.417 --> 00:22:37.917
<i>Until I touched it with my own hands</i>

00:22:37.917 --> 00:22:43.417
<i>I'll gather up</i>
<i>and go through all of the things</i>

00:22:43.417 --> 00:23:02.059
<i>Scattered beneath the waning moon</i>
